---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About | Soha Sami">
  <section class="inner-hero shell" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow">About Soha</p>
    <h1>Economics.<br />Mathematics.<br /><em>Energy.</em></h1>
  </section>

  <section class="about-intro shell" data-reveal>
    <div class="about-intro-label">
      <span>01</span>
      <p>Background</p>
    </div>

    <div class="about-intro-copy">
      <p class="about-lead">
        I’m Soha, a student working across energy markets, quantitative finance and climate risk.
      </p>

      <p>
        I’m currently studying through the Erasmus Mundus GrEnFin programme in
        Greening Energy Market and Finance, alongside an MSc in Financial and
        Insurance Mathematics at LMU Munich.
      </p>

      <p>
        My studies have taken me between Italy, France and Germany. Moving
        between Bologna, Paris and Munich has given me the chance to experience
        different academic environments as well as different perspectives on
        energy, finance and the industries around them.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="education-section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
        <span class="section-number">02</span>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Education</p>
          <h2>What I study.</h2>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="education-list">
        <article class="education-item" data-reveal>
          <div class="education-year">2025–2027</div>
          <div class="education-content">
            <p class="education-type">CURRENT · ERASMUS MUNDUS</p>
            <h3>Erasmus Mundus GrEnFin</h3>
            <h4>Greening Energy Market and Finance</h4>
            <p>
              GrEnFin is my main focus on energy markets and finance. My studies
              cover electricity markets, energy finance, climate and business,
              market design and the changes taking place across European energy
              systems.
            </p>
            <div class="education-universities">
              <span>Università di Bologna</span>
              <span>Université Paris Dauphine-PSL</span>
              <span>LMU Munich</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="education-item" data-reveal>
          <div class="education-year">2025–2027</div>
          <div class="education-content">
            <p class="education-type">CURRENT · MUNICH</p>
            <h3>MSc Financial and Insurance Mathematics</h3>
            <h4>Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München</h4>
            <p>
              At LMU, I am developing the mathematical side of my work through
              stochastic modelling, quantitative risk management, financial
              mathematics, numerical methods and statistical modelling.
            </p>
            <div class="education-tags">
              <span>Stochastic Modelling</span>
              <span>Quantitative Risk</span>
              <span>Financial Mathematics</span>
              <span>Numerical Methods</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="education-item" data-reveal>
          <div class="education-year">2021–2025</div>
          <div class="education-content">
            <p class="education-type">FOUNDATION · NEW DELHI</p>
            <h3>BA Economics & Mathematics</h3>
            <h4>University of Delhi</h4>
            <p>
              My bachelor's degree gave me the foundation in economics,
              mathematics, statistics and quantitative analysis that I now
              bring into my graduate work.
            </p>
            <div class="education-tags">
              <span>Economics</span>
              <span>Mathematics</span>
              <span>Statistics</span>
              <span>Quantitative Analysis</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="journey-section"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head" data-reveal><span class="section-number">03</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Academic journey</p><h2>Bologna → Paris → <em>Munich</em></h2></div></div><div class="journey-grid"><div class="journey-place" data-reveal><span>01</span><h3>Bologna</h3><p>Energy markets & finance</p><small>Università di Bologna</small></div><div class="journey-place active" data-reveal><span>02</span><h3>Paris</h3><p>Climate & Business</p><small>Université Paris Dauphine-PSL · Current</small></div><div class="journey-place" data-reveal><span>03</span><h3>Munich</h3><p>Financial & Insurance Mathematics</p><small>LMU Munich</small></div></div><div class="journey-copy" data-reveal><p>Living and studying in Italy, France and Germany has given me a chance to experience different academic environments and different perspectives on energy and finance. I am currently in Paris at Université Paris Dauphine-PSL.</p></div></div></section>

  <section class="about-focus-section">
    <div class="shell about-focus-grid">
      <div data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">What I am learning</p>
        <h2>What I am<br /><em>working on.</em></h2>
      </div>

      <div class="focus-columns" data-reveal>
        <div>
          <span>ENERGY</span>
          <p>Electricity markets</p>
          <p>Market design</p>
          <p>Renewable generation</p>
          <p>Flexibility</p>
          <p>Power price dynamics</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>QUANTITATIVE</span>
          <p>Stochastic modelling</p>
          <p>Quantitative risk management</p>
          <p>Numerical methods</p>
          <p>Monte Carlo simulation</p>
          <p>Dependence modelling</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>COMPUTATIONAL</span>
          <p>Python</p>
          <p>Statistical analysis</p>
          <p>Data pipelines</p>
          <p>Git & GitHub</p>
          <p>Reproducible research</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="scholarship-section">
    <div class="shell scholarship-grid" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Erasmus Mundus</p>
        <h2>Studying across<br /><em>Europe.</em></h2>
      </div>

      <div>
        <p class="scholarship-title">
          Erasmus Mundus Joint Master in Greening Energy Market and Finance
        </p>
        <p>
          The Erasmus Mundus scholarship made this international academic path
          possible and has allowed me to study in different European
          environments while focusing on energy markets, finance and the energy
          transition.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-end shell" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow">Currently</p>
    <h2>Energy markets, quantitative finance,<br /><em>and climate risk.</em></h2>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

